BT 0.15 0.30 0.60 rg /F2 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50.00 730.00 Tm (Cache Line \(Block\):) Tj ET
BT 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg /F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 190.00 730.00 Tm (The atomic block of data transferred between main memory and cache. Sizes are always powers of two \(e.g., 4B, 8B, 16B, 64B\).) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.30 0.60 rg /F2 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50.00 705.00 Tm (Tag Field:) Tj ET
BT 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg /F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 190.00 705.00 Tm (Upper address bits stored alongside cached data to uniquely identify which memory block is currently occupying the line.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.30 0.60 rg /F2 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50.00 680.00 Tm (Valid Bit \(V\):) Tj ET
BT 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg /F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 190.00 680.00 Tm (A 1-bit hardware flag. V=1 indicates the line contains valid initialized memory data; V=0 indicates unallocated / dirty state.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.30 0.60 rg /F2 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50.00 655.00 Tm (Index / Set Index:) Tj ET
BT 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg /F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 190.00 655.00 Tm (Middle address bits that select which specific cache line \(direct mapping\) or set \(set associative mapping\) the block maps to.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.30 0.60 rg /F2 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50.00 630.00 Tm (Block Offset:) Tj ET
BT 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg /F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 190.00 630.00 Tm (Lower address bits that select the exact byte within the multi-byte cache block.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.30 0.60 rg /F2 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50.00 605.00 Tm (Cache Hit:) Tj ET
BT 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg /F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 190.00 605.00 Tm (Condition where the requested memory address tag matches a valid tag in the addressed cache set. Low latency retrieval.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.30 0.60 rg /F2 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50.00 580.00 Tm (Cache Miss:) Tj ET
BT 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg /F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 190.00 580.00 Tm (Condition where the requested memory block is not found in cache. Data must be fetched from higher-latency DRAM.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.30 0.60 rg /F2 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 50.00 555.00 Tm (Compulsory \(Cold\) Miss:) Tj ET
