BT 0.10 0.25 0.60 rg /F2 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50.00 540.00 Tm (Viva Voce Examination Questions & Answers \(Frequently Asked Questions\):) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.30 0.60 rg /F2 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 55.00 515.00 Tm (Q1: Why must block size and cache size be powers of two?) Tj ET
BT 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 65.00 502.00 Tm (A1: Powers of two allow the hardware to extract offset, index, and tag fields using simple bitwise masking and shifts \(O\(1\) logic gates\) rather than costly division and remainder circuits.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.30 0.60 rg /F2 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 55.00 477.00 Tm (Q2: Why does a cache hit NOT reset or update the FIFO queue?) Tj ET
BT 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 65.00 464.00 Tm (A2: First-In First-Out strictly tracks the chronological arrival \(insertion\) of blocks into cache lines. Hit count or reference recency is completely ignored in FIFO; updating recency on hits is the core definition of LRU.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.30 0.60 rg /F2 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 55.00 439.00 Tm (Q3: What are the primary trade-offs between Direct and 4-Way Set Associative caches?) Tj ET
BT 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 65.00 426.00 Tm (A3: Direct mapping requires only 1 comparator and offers the fastest access time, but suffers from high conflict misses. 4-way set associative requires 4 comparators and slightly more routing area, but drastically reduces conflict misses.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.30 0.60 rg /F2 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 55.00 401.00 Tm (Q4: Explain how backward navigation \('Previous Step'\) is implemented.) Tj ET
BT 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 65.00 388.00 Tm (A4: For every simulated access, the engine records an immutable deep snapshot of all cache lines \(valid bit, tag, block\) and running statistics. Navigating backward restores the exact recorded snapshot rather than guessing.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.30 0.60 rg /F2 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 55.00 363.00 Tm (Q5: What is Belady's Anomaly and does it affect LRU?) Tj ET
BT 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 65.00 350.00 Tm (A5: Belady's Anomaly is a counter-intuitive phenomenon where increasing cache capacity leads to more misses. It can occur in FIFO, but is mathematically impossible in LRU because LRU belongs to the class of 'Stack Algorithms'.) Tj ET
